Moscow is trying to claim these four  regions of Ukraine as part of Russia  following staged referendums that were  widely criticized as a sham even though  Ukraine and its allies refused to  recognize the regions as anything but  Ukrainian Russia's attempted land grab  has helped usher in a new and  potentially more dangerous phase of the  war here's why  the four regions where the staged votes  took place are crucial to Russia's war  strategy luhansk Donetsk zapparija and  Herson cementing control of them would  help Russia secure its desired land  bridge to Crimea which Russia annexed in  2014 after holding the same kind of  widely criticized process holding these  territories would also help choke  Ukraine's economy off from Key waterways  plus Russia has stated that the quote  liberation of the Don boss which  includes luhansk and Donetsk is a top  objective right now all four regions are  under at least partial Russian control  and ahead of the vote pro-russian  propaganda filled the streets people  passed out pamphlets and billboards  plugged things like Russian payouts to  mothers for having kids Russian  traditions and values like marriage and  Russian history which this sign says  cannot be canceled as for the so-called  voting video shows armed guards  overseeing the process in some places  and residents appeared to cast ballads  in the open before stuffing them into  see-through ballot boxes some people  said they were being threatened and told  that voting was mandatory regardless of  the results some analysts say that  Russia could lose some or all of this  territory to Ukrainian forces who have  gained momentum and retaken critical  areas in recent weeks Russia's new  territorial claims aren't likely to  change Ukraine's strategy that's  according to my colleague Ian who's been  in Europe covering the conflict I spoken  to military officials from Ukraine who  say these votes which they call fake  referendums will have no bearing at all  on the way we're conducting our military  operation so if Ukrainian forces aren't  changing course why do the so-called  referendums matter they're important to  the Kremlin and President Vladimir Putin  for a few reasons first they could help  Putin justify a full military draft down  the road if he chooses to call one and  they support his case for the partial  mobilization he announced before the  vote  which he says is necessary to protect  Russia's sovereignty and territorial  Integrity the announcement prompted some  Russians to leave the country but if  Russia says that these four regions are  Russian it can justify sending  conscripts in to try and fight to defend  them and these regions make up 15  percent of Ukraine's territory so  military analysts say Russia will need a  lot of support if it wants to try and  hold the line secondly the staged  referendums could help appease some  hardliners in Russia who have grown  critical of the Kremlin strategy after  humiliating setbacks many of them have  called for a full-scale war and even  retaliatory strikes against NATO members  who are backing Ukraine the criticism is  posing a fresh challenge for Putin who  has tried to silence any backlash  against the war third the referendums  could open the door to a bigger and more  dangerous conflict around the same time  that the staged voting process and  mobilization were announced Putin  pledged to use all means at Russia's  disposal including nuclear weapons to  defend its territorial Integrity  Putin could try to use the staged  referendums and the nuclear threats to  negotiate an end to the war on his terms  even though Ukrainian president  velodimir zielinski has said he won't  negotiate until all Russian forces have  left Ukrainian land we can return the  Ukrainian flag to our entire territory  we can do it with the force of arms but  perhaps an even bigger priority for  Putin is to get the West to back off its  support of Ukraine it's the Western Arms  that have really turned the time of the  war it's these long-range Rockets mostly  from the U.S have allowed them to really  push Russia back and so he he's trying  to frighten Western allies away from  continuing to give support to Ukraine  it's too early to say if his actions  will have an impact but for now Western  leaders are calling for more sanctions  against Russia and expressing even  greater support for Ukraine
 

